@startuml
title `5 / 0` — one term, three execution lanes, three different (and each correct) dispositions

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam ParticipantPadding 14
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam participant {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

participant "**source text**\n`5 / 0`" as SRC #DCFCE7
participant "**wpda.rs**\nWPDA parser" as PARSE #DCFCE7
participant "**safeify**\n`macros/src/gen/native/`\n`rust_code_rewrite.rs`" as SAFE #EDE9FE
participant "**SafeArith**\n`runtime/src/safe_arith.rs`\n`safe_div` = `checked_div`" as ARITH #EDE9FE
participant "**eval.rs**\ndirect evaluation" as EVAL #FEF3C7
participant "**dovetail_report.rs**\ne-graph saturation" as DOVE #FCE7F3
participant "**rho_fold_dataflow.rs**\nRho-machine lowering" as RHO #FCE7F3

SRC -> PARSE : token stream `5` `/` `0`
PARSE -> SAFE : ""DivInt(NumLit(5), NumLit(0))""\n(parsing ALWAYS succeeds — partiality is\na REDUCTION property, not a syntax one)

note over SAFE
  The declared body is `![a / b]`. `safeify` rewrote it at
  macro-expansion time into
  <latex>\mathtt{SafeArith::safe\_div}(a,b)\;?</latex>
  so the `?` short-circuits the whole body to `None`.
end note

SAFE -> ARITH : ""safe_div(5, 0)""
ARITH --> SAFE : ""None""   (<latex>\mathtt{checked\_div}</latex> is `None` on a zero divisor,\nand on <latex>i32{::}\mathrm{MIN} / (-1)</latex>)

group Lane 1 — direct evaluation (`Int::eval` / `Int::try_eval`)
  SAFE -> EVAL : the arm returns `None`
  EVAL --> EVAL : ""try_eval()"" yields ""None""
  EVAL --> EVAL : ""eval()"" is ""try_eval().expect(…)""\n<b>⇒ PANIC</b>: "Cannot evaluate expression …"
end

group Lane 2 — e-graph saturation (Dovetail)
  SAFE -> DOVE : the native dispatcher arm returns `None`
  DOVE --> DOVE : the fold rule DOES NOT FIRE —\nno new e-class is added
  DOVE --> DOVE : ""DivInt(NumLit 5, NumLit 0)"" is a\n<b>STUCK TERM</b>: a normal form with no value
end

group Lane 3 — the Rho machine (production `exec`)
  SAFE -> RHO : lowering attempt
  RHO --> RHO : disposition =\n""BlockedBySemanticPredicate(SafeEvaluationDeclined)""
  RHO --> RHO : the report-free fast path DEFERS; the wrapper\nLAZILY builds the checked Dovetail report as the\n<b>observational payload</b> (backend `Dovetail`,\nartifact `DovetailRunReport`)
end

note over EVAL, RHO
  **Nothing anywhere produces an error TERM.** `Int::Err` (surface `error`)
  and `CastErrInt` (surface `cast_error_int`) are PARSEABLE, INERT normal
  forms; the generated Calculator constructs neither. `Int::Err` is pushed
  only by the WPDA literal action when the token `error` is read, and
  `CastResult::err()` — the sink that would produce them — is emitted only
  for OBJECT-output cast languages. Calculator's casts are all
  NATIVE-output, which "defers on `None`".
end note

@enduml
